+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` walks a pair's closed trades backwards from the most recent one and counts
+how many resulted in a loss (profit below `required_profit`) in an unbroken row. Once
+`max_consecutive_losses` losses have happened back-to-back for that pair, the pair is locked for
+`stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set
+time when using `unlock_at`) - regardless of how long the streak took to develop, since (unlike
+most other Protections) this one ignores `lookback_period`.
+
+By default, the same streak is also evaluated across all pairs combined (a loss on one pair
+followed immediately by a loss on another still counts towards the bot-wide streak), locking all
+pairs once the bot-wide streak reaches `max_consecutive_losses`. Set `only_per_pair` to `true` to
+disable this bot-wide lock and only ever lock the individual pair.
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side (long/short),
+and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a streak of
+losing longs.
+
+The below example locks a pair (and, since `only_per_pair` defaults to `false`, the whole bot)
+for 12 candles after 3 losing trades happened back-to-back.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "max_consecutive_losses": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
