+  location: max_consecutive_losses.py
+  annotations: |
+    Locks trading (globally or per-pair) once the most recent closed trades — for the pair, or
+    across all pairs — form an unbroken streak of `max_consecutive_losses` losses in a row.
+    Unlike `StoplossGuard`/`LowProfitPairs`, the streak is not bounded by `lookback_period`;
+    it walks the closed-trade history backwards from the newest trade until a non-loss breaks
+    the streak. One of several concrete handlers in this cell; see `extension_point`.
